---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { posts } from '../data/posts.js';

const latestPosts = posts.slice(0, 3);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Thanks for reaching out | 22 Local Marketing"
  description="We received your request and will be in touch within one business day."
>
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow" slot="head" />

  <!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
  <header class="ty-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="ty-hero-inner">
        <div class="eyebrow-rugged">
          <span class="eb-dash"></span>
          <span>Request received</span>
        </div>
        <h1>Thanks. We got your request.</h1>
        <p class="ty-sub">We will go through your market, your site, and your current Google presence before we call, so the first conversation is a useful one. Expect to hear from Connor within one business day.</p>
        <div class="ty-actions">
          <a href="/blog/" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Read the blog <span class="btn-arrow">&#8594;</span></a>
          <a href="/" class="btn btn-secondary btn-lg">Back to home</a>
        </div>
        <p class="ty-note">Need us sooner? Call or text <a href="tel:+18653483380">(865) 348-3380</a>, or email <a href="mailto:connor@22localmarketing.com">connor@22localmarketing.com</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- ============ WHAT HAPPENS NEXT ============ -->
  <section class="flush">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>What happens next.</h2>
        <span class="desc">Three steps, and none of them need anything from you today.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ty-steps">
        <div class="ty-step">
          <div class="ty-step-num">01</div>
          <div class="ty-step-title">We look first</div>
          <div class="ty-step-body">We go through your website, Google Business Profile, ads, and reviews before we pick up the phone. That way we come in with specifics instead of questions you have already answered.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="ty-step">
          <div class="ty-step-num">02</div>
          <div class="ty-step-title">We call you</div>
          <div class="ty-step-body">Connor reaches out within one business day. You get our read on your market and where the clearest opportunities are, whether or not we end up working together.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="ty-step">
          <div class="ty-step-num">03</div>
          <div class="ty-step-title">You decide</div>
          <div class="ty-step-body">If it makes sense on both sides, we scope the work and give you a flat number. If it does not, we will tell you that too and point you somewhere better.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ FAQ ============ -->
  <section id="faq">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Questions that usually come up next.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <div class="faq-item open"><button class="faq-q">How long until I see results?</button><div class="faq-a">Expect 3 to 5 leads in the first couple of months, and growth from there. Paid usually moves first because you're buying placement. Map pack movement tends to show up inside 30 to 60 days. Organic ranking shifts take 3 to 6 months depending on where you're starting. We'll give you our read on your specific market on the first call rather than a generic number.</div></div>
        <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">I've tried a marketing agency before and it didn't work. Why would this be different?</button><div class="faq-a">That's the objection we hear most, and it's usually earned. Here's what we can point at instead of arguing. Our clients average 60-plus phone calls and 40-plus form leads a month at under $50 per lead. One land management client in Northwest Ohio went from no search presence at all to ranking for over 1,000 queries, with 160-plus of them in Google's top three, inside six months. Our own profile sits at 5.0 stars across 36 verified Google reviews.<br><br>Now the honest part. Expect 3 to 5 leads in the first couple of months, then building from there. Not fifty. If someone promises you fifty in month one, that's the version of this that didn't work last time.</div></div>
        <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">Do I own the website and accounts you build?</button><div class="faq-a">Yes. You own the website, the domain, the GBP, the ad accounts, the call tracking, and everything in between. If we ever part ways, you walk with everything.</div></div>
        <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">What does it actually cost?</button><div class="faq-a">Engagements are scoped to the work and your market. Most full-service clients land in the range you'd expect for an in-house marketing hire, but with a whole team behind it. We give you a flat number on the second call once we understand the scope.</div></div>
        <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">Will you work with my existing website?</button><div class="faq-a">Sometimes yes. If the bones are good, we tune it. If it's holding you back, we rebuild it. The audit tells us which one. Most clients end up with a rebuild because the gap to top-of-industry is bigger than it looks from the inside.</div></div>
        <div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q">Do you only work with tree and land companies?</button><div class="faq-a">That's where we focus, and it's where most of our clients are. The playbook came out of tree care and land management, so we know the search terms, the seasonality, and the way these jobs get bought.<br><br>We do take on other home service contractors when the fit is right. Electrical, plumbing, HVAC, roofing, landscaping, grading, and similar trades all run on the same method, since the lead is a phone call and the job happens at a property. Ask on the first call and we'll tell you whether we're the right fit.</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ============ BLOG ============ -->
  <section id="reading">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>Worth a read while you wait.</h2>
        <span class="desc">The same thinking we bring to client campaigns, written down.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ty-post-grid">
        {latestPosts.map((post) => (
          <a class="ty-post" href={`/blog/${post.slug}/`}>
            <div class="ty-post-meta">
              <span class="ty-post-cat">{post.category}</span>
              <span class="ty-post-read">{post.readTime}</span>
            </div>
            <h3>{post.title}</h3>
            <p>{post.excerpt}</p>
            <span class="ty-post-link">Read article <span class="btn-arrow">&#8594;</span></span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="ty-post-all">
        <a href="/blog/" class="btn btn-secondary">See all articles <span class="btn-arrow">&#8594;</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
/* ===== HERO ===== */
.ty-hero { padding: 150px 0 80px; background: var(--white); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
.ty-hero-inner { max-width: 760px; }
.ty-hero h1 {
  font-size: clamp(34px, 5vw, 54px); line-height: 1.08; font-weight: 700;
  letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin: 20px 0 18px;
}
.ty-sub { font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--slate); max-width: 620px; }
.ty-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 32px; }
.ty-note { margin-top: 26px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--slate-light); }
.ty-note a { color: var(--onyx); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
.ty-note a:hover { color: var(--blaze); }

/* ===== STEPS ===== */
.ty-steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; }
.ty-step {
  background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px;
  padding: 26px 24px; transition: border-color 0.15s, transform 0.15s;
}
.ty-step:hover { border-color: var(--onyx); transform: translateY(-2px); }
.ty-step-num { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--blaze); letter-spacing: 0.08em; }
.ty-step-title { font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.01em; margin: 10px 0 8px; }
.ty-step-body { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--slate); }

/* ===== FAQ (mirrors the homepage accordion) ===== */
.faq-list { display: grid; gap: 12px; max-width: 880px; margin: 0 auto; }
.faq-item {
  background: var(--white); border: 1px solid var(--onyx); border-radius: 8px;
  overflow: hidden; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 0 var(--onyx);
  transition: transform 0.15s, box-shadow 0.15s;
}
.faq-item:hover { transform: translate(-2px, -2px); box-shadow: 6px 6px 0 0 var(--onyx); }
.faq-q {
  width: 100%; text-align: left; background: none; border: 0; cursor: pointer;
  padding: 20px 24px; font-family: inherit; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em; color: var(--onyx);
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px;
}
.faq-q::after { content: '+'; font-family: 'Sora', sans-serif; font-size: 22px; color: var(--blaze); transition: transform 0.2s; line-height: 1; }
.faq-item.open .faq-q::after { content: '\2013'; }
.faq-a { padding: 0 24px 22px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--slate); line-height: 1.6; display: none; }
.faq-item.open .faq-a { display: block; }

/* ===== BLOG ===== */
.ty-post-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 16px; }
.ty-post {
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; background: var(--white);
  border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 24px;
  text-decoration: none; color: inherit; transition: border-color 0.15s, transform 0.15s;
}
.ty-post:hover { border-color: var(--onyx); transform: translateY(-2px); }
.ty-post-meta { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; font-size: 12px; color: var(--slate-light); }
.ty-post-cat { color: var(--blaze); font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase; }
.ty-post h3 { font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.01em; line-height: 1.3; margin: 12px 0 10px; }
.ty-post p { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--slate); margin-bottom: 18px; }
.ty-post-link { margin-top: auto; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--onyx); }
.ty-post:hover .ty-post-link { color: var(--blaze); }
.ty-post-all { display: flex; justify-content: center; margin-top: 28px; }

@media (max-width: 900px) {
  .ty-steps, .ty-post-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .ty-hero { padding: 120px 0 64px; }
}
</style>

<script is:inline>
document.querySelectorAll('.faq-q').forEach(btn => {
  btn.addEventListener('click', () => btn.parentElement.classList.toggle('open'));
});
</script>
